{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvam46gcWyiZwErHc5MK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**I'd skip the broad non-buyer survey and first look at why buyers asked for refunds. Don't decide on price yet.**\n\n**Why the survey is the wrong first step**\n- **The gap is too big for price to explain.** 0.3% against a 3% target is a 10× miss. Cutting £15 to, say, £8 is very unlikely to produce a 10× lift. Something more basic is probably wrong, such as the need, the offer's visibility or the positioning.\n- **Non-buyers' answers are weak evidence.** Stated willingness to pay is unreliable, and most of them probably never seriously considered the offer. They'll say \"cheaper\" because it's an easy answer.\n- **The refund rate is the bigger signal.** 40% of the few people who wanted it then reversed. That points to a mismatch between the promise and the delivery, or to buyer's remorse. A lower price wouldn't fix that, and it would make the add-on's economics worse.\n\n**What I'd do instead**\n1. **Check the numbers.** If the treatment arm was about 10,000, that's roughly 30 buyers and about 12 refunds. That's a small sample, so treat the rates as rough. Net retained take-up is about 0.18%.\n2. **Look at the funnel.** Find out how many people saw the offer, clicked and reached checkout, and where they dropped off. Low visibility and low interest need different fixes.\n3. **Talk to the refunders and buyers.** Ask what they expected and what they got. A dozen conversations will probably teach more than thousands of survey responses.\n4. **Interview or survey a small, targeted group.** That means heavy support users, not all non-buyers. Ask about actual support pain, not hypothetical pricing.\n5. **Only then test price, if the evidence points that way.** Run a randomised test with two or three price points and a clear description of what's included. That would give real behavioural evidence on price.\n\nI'd call this a reshape: the offer's value and expectations need work before price is worth testing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3450,"cache_read_input_tokens":5010,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3450},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2dc377de-34c4-4bec-b63b-f6e83f1f3fda","uuid":"2f2712aa-5d80-4061-938e-a5ac0cd9dc2d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:09:49.448Z","request_id":"req_011Cfvam3rJKw8DrYsAAHSHa"}
